.TH DEB-MANAGER-GUI 1 "2026-11-17" "deb-manager-gui 1.0.0" "Mainuan"
.SH NAME
deb-manager-gui \- graphical progress window for APT package operations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deb-manager-gui
.RB { \-\-in | \-\-rm }
.I package
.RI [ package ...]
.RB [ \-\-tx
.IR message ]
.br
.B deb-manager-gui \-\-deb
.I file.deb
.RI [ file.deb ...]
.RB [ \-\-tx
.IR message ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B deb-manager-gui
installs or removes packages with
.BR apt-get (8),
or installs local files with
.BR dpkg (1),
while a Qt window shows the progress. A message box reports success or
failure at the end.
.PP
It is meant to be started by other programs through
.BR pkexec (1).
When it is not running as root, the package tools are called through
.BR sudo (8).
The package tools run without interactive questions and keep existing
configuration files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-in
Install the named packages from the configured APT repositories.
.TP
.B \-\-rm
Remove the named packages.
.TP
.B \-\-deb
Install local .deb files; missing dependencies are then resolved with
.BR "apt-get \-f install" .
.TP
.BI \-\-tx " message"
Text shown in the window instead of the package list. Everything after
.B \-\-tx
is part of the message.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The interface follows
.BR LANGUAGE " and " LANG .
Under
.BR pkexec (1),
which clears the environment, the language of the calling user's Plasma
session (~/.config/plasma-localerc) or /etc/default/locale is used.
.SH EXAMPLE
pkexec deb-manager-gui \-\-in vlc \-\-tx "Installing the media player"
